AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     Implemented by Steve Casner based on an initial prototype written by Ajit
     Thyagarajan.  The multicast traceroute mechanism was designed by Van
     Jacobson with help from Steve Casner, Steve Deering, Dino Farinacci, and
     Deb Agrawal; it was implemented in mmrroouutteedd by Ajit Thyagarajan and Bill
     Fenner.  The option syntax and the output format of mmttrraaccee are modeled
     after the unicast traceroute(8) program written by Van Jacobson.

BBUUGGSS
     Versions 3.3 and 3.5 of mmrroouutteedd will crash if a trace query is received
     via a unicast packet and mmrroouutteedd has no route for the _s_o_u_r_c_e address.
     Therefore, do not use the --gg option unless the target mmrroouutteedd has been
     verified to be 3.4 or newer than 3.5.

